    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d720">

                <pb facs="0974" n="860" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg860"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.632/91: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stockton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-02-17T13:00:00+01:00">February 17, 1931—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 17—10:30 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>9. Refer to Department’s telegram No. 4 of February 16.<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d720-f1"/> Today Schober wanted to know what the prospects were of
                    Senate acting this session. Fear that Austrian Government is stalling while
                    awaiting Senate action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d720-f1" n="15" xml:id="d720-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it stated that the President had sent the supplementary agreement to
                    the Senate on February 14 (711.632/89).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
